        "result": "Fetched ex parte/due counts: March 2026 8,103/19,890; April 8,739/20,186; May 6,914/16,265; June 5,501/15,157. Computed shares rounded to one decimal: 40.7%, 43.3%, 42.5%, 36.3%. June also reports 9,256 total renewed and 498 pending."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The reference class and base rate are twelve distinct monthly Delaware O rows from July 2025 through June 2026. Their unweighted mean share is 43.6220%; the January-June mean is 41.9074%; June is 36.2935%. These are state-level original-submission rates, not national totals or updated (U) outcomes. Historical O rows were fetched from the current September 2026 release; archived first-publication vintages were not independently checked."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Verification limitation: the official snapshot release page lists January-June 2026 publications on April 24, May 29, June 26, July 31, August 28, and September 25, respectively. No official future publication schedule verifying December 15, 2026 was found. The resolutionDate remains the registered contract date, not a verified CMS publication date; the prompt's release-date verification requirement therefore remains unmet. An initial web lookup failed, but subsequent official CMS API fetches successfully supplied the history."
      },
      {
        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use a judgmental persistence prior with partial mean reversion: 75% of June's unrounded rate plus 25% of the twelve-month mean. Starting from the 43.6220% base rate, the latest-level adjustment is 0.75*(36.2935-43.6220) = -5.4964 percentage points. Momentum, one-off, and policy-mechanism adjustments are each zero: observed changes reverse direction, the termination-hold footnote recurs throughout the sample, and no quantified August-specific policy break was established. Point = 43.6220-5.4964 = 38.1256%, rounded to 38.1%. For eleven successive unrounded monthly changes, sum(delta) = -8.778419 and sum(delta^2) = 334.177509. sigma = 5.7199 percentage points, calculated as sqrt((334.177509-(-8.778419)^2/11)/10). The one-month nominal 80% half-width is 1.28*sigma = 7.3215 points. Scale by sqrt(2) for the two reporting-month horizon from June to August: half-width = 10.3541 points. Bounds = 38.1256 +/- 10.3541 = 27.7715 to 48.4797%, rounded to 27.8%-48.5%. This model-based interval assumes independent monthly innovations; its empirical coverage has not been validated."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Upside risk: an August cohort with more successful automated eligibility matches could raise the share; repeating August 2025's fetched 51.8% would land above the interval. Downside risk: more beneficiaries requiring forms, becoming disenrolled, or remaining pending could lower the ex parte share. A sustained operational disruption producing a share below 27.8% would fall outside the interval. One observed August does not establish a repeatable seasonal adjustment."
      },
